reviews.text_contribution:
The manuscript studies eight common classifier-based uncertainty quantification (UQ) techniques for out-of-distribution (OOD) detection on three fetal ultrasound datasets and provide two major findings:
(1) the OOD performance of a UQ-model depends on both the classification task, and the type of distribution shift;
(2) the OOD performance does not imply the best abstinence performance.

